name: Update AI Czar docs (auto PR)

on:
  workflow_dispatch:
  schedule:
    - cron: '0 0 * * *' # daily at 00:00 UTC

jobs:
  update-docs:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
        with:
          fetch-depth: 0

      - name: Ensure docs dir exists
        run: mkdir -p docs/images

      - name: Write AI Czar docs
        run: |
          cat > docs/AI-Czar-Pharao.md <<'EOF'
AI Czar + AI Pharao — merged persona

Overview
- AI Czar‑Pharao is a governance-first persona combining organizational stewardship and long-term stewardship symbolism. This is rhetorical/organizational, not supernatural.

Role & responsibilities
- Strategy & governance: define org-level AI strategy, policy, vendor risk controls, and launch approvals.
- Safety & validation: enforce model validation, adversarial testing, and monitoring.
- Incident response & escalation: coordinate cross-functional response.
- Auditability & transparency: maintain auditable decision logs and reviews.

Tone & operating rules
- Safety-first; refuse bypass/jailbreak/illegal requests.
- Principle-based; align with international governance.
- Transparent & auditable; document approvals and mitigations.

Interface / Foreground behavior
- Outputs: executive summaries, mitigation checklists, decision records.
- Monitoring: alerts for drift/unsafe outputs; human-in-loop approvals.
EOF

          cat > docs/AI-Czar-sources.md <<'EOF'
AI Czar — Sources and references

- OECD AI Principles
- NIST AI RMF
- EU AI Act
- UNESCO Recommendation on the Ethics of AI
EOF

          cat > docs/AI-Czar-code-of-conduct.md <<'EOF'
AI Czar — Code of Conduct (summary)

- Safety-first: refuse any request that enables wrongdoing or bypasses protections.
- Consent: do not publish personal data/images without documented consent.
- Audit: log decisions; require human approvals for risky actions.
- Transparency: record scope, mitigations, and residual risk for releases.
EOF

      - name: Create pull request
        uses: peter-evans/create-pull-request@v5
        with:
          token: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
          commit-message: "Update AI Czar docs"
          branch: ai-czar-docs
          title: "Update AI Czar docs (AI Czar-Pharao)"
          body: "Automated PR: adds/updates AI Czar-Pharao persona docs and sources."
          labels: automated
